.TH CTPOOL_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_shutdown_drain \- graceful shutdown
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadpool.h>

void ctpool_shutdown_drain(ctpool pool);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Tells the pool to accept no new task, waits for every task in the queue
and every active task to finish, and then joins every worker thread.
The call blocks until every worker has exited.

The pool accepts no new task after this call returns, and ctpool_destroy
can then free the pool struct.

A second call, whether it follows the first one or runs at the same time
on another thread, does no more shutdown work of its own, but it still
blocks until the shutdown that is already under way stops. Every caller
therefore gets the same guarantee: after the call returns, every worker
thread has exited.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pool   Thread pool handle (CTPOOL_INVALID or a stale/already-destroyed
       handle is a no-op)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Every submit function returns ccol_not_permitted after this call, with
one exception: ctpool_submit_future, which reports a failure only as a
NULL return.
The library wakes every thread that blocks in ctpool_submit on a full
bounded queue, and each of them receives ccol_not_permitted.

A call to ctpool_shutdown_drain on pool from inside a task that runs on
one of the worker threads of pool, or from the on_complete callback of
that task, does nothing at all. It neither stops the pool from
accepting new tasks nor joins any worker, and it does not block. A
worker thread cannot join itself, so going ahead could never wait for
the calling thread to exit; it could only wait for every other worker.

A ctpool_shutdown_immediate call can arrive while this call still
drains. That call then takes over: it discards whatever is still in the
queue at that moment and cancels the futures of those tasks, and this
call returns after every worker has exited.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_shutdown_immediate (3),
.BR ctpool_wait (3),
.BR ctpool_destroy (3)
